{
  "_note": "Wayback 20251225201749 (13:17 MST): snow-reports (report[0] = Dec 25; report[1] = Dec 20, kept for the O12 test: overnight 3 vs computed 24_hour 0), lifts, sensors, trails. No terrains capture that day. Trimmed to the fields snowbird.ts reads.",
  "report": [
    {"date":"2025-12-25 05:43:26","updated":1766667850,"overnight_amount":2,"base_depth":28,"computed":{"24_hour":2,"48_hour":2,"72_hour":2,"7_day":5,"total":57},"report":"<p dir=\"ltr\">Merry Christmas Snowbird! It’s Owen, with your holiday snow report.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">It is finally Christmas and it looks like at least one person asked for snow because we got 2” overnight. That’ll give us a nice little padding going into today with snow showers forecast until 11 am, then a chance of snow from then until 2 pm. We will have a high of around 42° and a chance of thunder throughout the day so keep an eye out for alerts from the Snowbird App on any potential closures. The snow will be skiing nice and soft today, it should be a fun one.&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">What did you guys get for Christmas? I got coal. I don’t want to talk about it.&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Kidding, I haven’t checked yet, but hopefully there is a really long box with skis inside hidden somewhere that I didn’t see before I left this morning. Anyways, no events today, so go enjoy some Christmas laps with family and friends, and have some hot chocolate and cookies for après.&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The Tram, Gadzoom, Wilbere, Chickadee and the Chickadee Conveyor will be running at 9 am, conditions permitting.&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">I know we are all stoked to be out on the mountain, but please remember that we have early-season conditions. Don’t be a grinch (I swear I saw him out on the mountain the other day) - please ski and ride with caution and stay in control. It’ll make the experience better for everyone. If you are looking for more Early Season information, <a href=\"https://www.snowbird.com/the-mountain/early-season/\">click here</a>.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">ALL uphill travel is closed for the season now that Snowbird is open for lift-service skiing and riding.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">It’s a good day up here, get up to the Bird! I’ll see you out there. Merry Christmas folks!</p>"},
    {"date":"2025-12-20 05:40:43","updated":1766258271,"overnight_amount":3,"base_depth":24,"computed":{"24_hour":0,"48_hour":0,"72_hour":0,"7_day":3,"total":55},"report":"<p>Hi fellow people who say \"Give me the Bird,\" it’s your once-a-week Snow Reporter, Jake.</p><p>I’ll keep this brief. Snowbird got fresh snow, and if you don’t plan to be at the resort today, then it’s time to reevaluate. Since 8 pm yesterday, Snowbird has picked up 3 inches, with more in the forcast.&nbsp;</p><p>If you have made the right decision and are brewing a “roadie” cup of coffee before hitting the road, today’s weather conditions call for overcast skies as the snow continues to fall into the afternoon. Temperatures will fluctuate in the mid-30s, with southwest winds gusting around 10 mhp.&nbsp;</p><p>The Aerial Tram, Gadzoom, Wilbere, Chickadee and the Chickadee Conveyor will all be running at 9 am, conditions permitting.&nbsp;</p><p>Early-season conditions exist. Please ski and ride with caution and be considerate of others on the slopes. <a href=\"https://www.snowbird.com/the-mountain/early-season/\">Click here</a> for more information.&nbsp;</p><p>Please note, The Summit restaurant is closed today.&nbsp;</p><p>What else is going on at The Bird? Well for starters, it’s the seventh day of Hanukkah.&nbsp;There will be a lighting ceremony at The Cliff Lodge Front Desk at 5 pm. Everyone is welcome, and you can also BYOM (bring your own menorah).&nbsp;</p><p>Looking forward, there are lots of things to do at Snowbird over the holiday period. From torchlight parades and candlelighting to Santa and fireworks, you don’t want to miss out. Visit the <a href=\"https://www.snowbird.com/activities-events/events/events-calendar/?filterEventType=&amp;gad_campaignid=21862871035&amp;gad_source=1&amp;gbraid=0AAAAACPbr9STVp9zkffYK1bN71Q26IlbY&amp;gclid=EAIaIQobChMIsabL4tDKkQMVXidECB3w6jqyEAAYASAAEgLN3fD_BwE&amp;gclsrc=aw.ds\">events webpage</a> for a full calendar and more information.&nbsp;</p><p>All uphill travel is CLOSED.</p>"}
  ],
